CM ============================================================
CM  TM-SC-NEC-003: Screwdriver Antenna — 15m Band
CM  2.4m whip, base loading coil, 4 horizontal elevated radials
CM  Frequency: 21.000–21.452 MHz (5 points, 0.113 MHz step)
CM
CM  Loading coil (series RL at base, segment 1 of GW1):
CM    R = 0.481 ohm  (Rcoil = Xant / Q, Q~360)
CM    X = 173.3 ohm  (XL required to resonate 2.4m whip on 15m)
CM
CM  Whip: 2.4m, avg radius 0.006m, 20 segments
CM  Radials: 4 x 2.4m at z=0.005m, 90 deg spacing
CM  Ground: real (Sommerfeld-Norton), eps=13, sigma=0.005
CM  Feed: 1V voltage source at GW1, seg 1
CM
CM  Tuning note: 15m is a primary DX band. Whip is electrically
CM  shorter than quarter-wave (3.57m at 21 MHz), so loading is
CM  moderate. Gain pattern shows low-angle radiation suitable
CM  for NVIS/DX blend depending on ground conditions.
